--- /dev/null
+++ b/tools/openvino/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,405 @@
+# GDRNPP OpenVINO Pipeline
+
+GDRNPP 6D pose estimation pipeline ported to Intel OpenVINO, enabling inference on Intel CPUs and GPUs without PyTorch/CUDA dependencies.
+
+## Architecture
+
+```
+Image ──► YOLOX (detection) ──► GDRN (pose estimation)
+                                       │
+                    outputs: 6D Poses(rot6d + trans) + coor_xyz + mask
+                                       │
+                              ┌────────┴────────┐
+                              ▼                 ▼
+                      Direct Regression      coor_xyz + mask
+                      (rot6d + trans)           │
+                              │                 ▼
+                              │            PnP RANSAC → rot6d + trans
+                              └─────┐
+                                    ▼
+                              Optional: Depth Refine ──► Refined 6D Poses
+```
+
+## Environment Setup
+
+The project ships a pre-configured Docker environment with OpenVINO, PyTorch 2.14 (CPU), Intel GPU drivers, Mesa and all dependencies.
+
+```bash
+# Build and start container (handles UID/GID, GPU passthrough automatically)
+bash docker_build_run.sh
+
+# Enter container
+docker exec -it gdrnpp_dev bash
+```
+
+Or step by step:
+
+```bash
+bash docker_build_run.sh --build-only   # build image only
+bash docker_build_run.sh --run-only     # start container only (image must exist)
+```
+
+Intel GPU access is passed through via `/dev/dri` with proper group permissions.
+After the container starts, `docker_build_run.sh` also compiles the
+Python 3.12-compatible `CppEGLRenderer` extension from the mounted source tree.
+This enables GPU-accelerated depth rendering for `--depth-refine`; if EGL cannot
+be initialized, the pipeline reports the error and falls back to the slower CPU
+renderer.
+
+### Lightweight Deployment
+
+Model conversion requires PyTorch and the full development environment, but
+deployment with exported OpenVINO IR files does not. Install the inference-only
+Python dependencies in a separate environment:
+
+```bash
+python3 -m venv .venv-deploy
+source .venv-deploy/bin/activate
+pip install -r requirements/requirements_deploy.txt
+```
+
+For `--depth-refine`, install the system OpenGL/EGL development libraries and
+compile the renderer once:
+
+```bash
+# Ubuntu 24.04
+sudo apt-get install build-essential cmake python3-dev libgl1-mesa-dev libegl1-mesa-dev
+bash lib/egl_renderer/compile_cpp_egl_renderer.sh
+```
+
+The deployment requirements intentionally exclude PyTorch, torchvision, mmcv,
+detectron2 and pyassimp. They support OpenVINO inference, YOLOX post-processing,
+and EGL depth refinement. The bundled BOP scorer is a development/evaluation
+tool with additional dependencies; use `--save-only` in the lightweight
+environment or score the generated CSV in the full environment.
+
+
+## Directory Layout
+
+```
+tools/openvino/
+├── README.md                    # this file
+├── export_yolox_openvino.py     # export YOLOX from PyTorch → OV IR
+├── export_gdrn_openvino.py      # export GDRN from PyTorch → OV IR
+├── gdrnpp_ov_pipeline.py        # main pipeline (GDRNPPPipeline class)
+├── eval_bop_openvino.py         # BOP evaluation driver
+└── infer_utils.py               # shared utilities (preproc, postproc, PnP)
+
+models/openvino/                 # exported IR files (not in git)
+├── yolox/
+│   └── yolox.xml / .bin
+└── gdrn/
+    └── gdrn.xml / .bin
+```
+
+## Usage
+
+### Step 1: Export Models
+
+#### YOLOX
+
+```bash
+python tools/openvino/export_yolox_openvino.py \
+    --ckpt output/yolox/.../model_final.pth \
+    --output models/openvino/<yolox_dir>
+```
+
+| Argument | Default | Description |
+|----------|---------|-------------|
+| `--ckpt` | (required) | Path to PyTorch checkpoint (.pth) |
+| `--output` | `models/openvino/yolox` | Output directory for IR files |
+| `--convert-mode` | `pytorch-ov` | Conversion path: `pytorch-onnx-ov` (via ONNX) or `pytorch-ov` (direct) |
+| `--dynamic` | off | Export with bounded dynamic batch `[1..max-batch]` |
+| `--max-batch` | `16` | Upper bound for dynamic batch dimension |
+| `--fp16` | off | Compress weights to FP16 |
+| `--verify` | off | Verify OV output against PyTorch |
+| `--input-size` | auto | Input H W (auto-detected from config if not set) |
+| `--num-classes` | auto | Number of detection classes (auto-detected from checkpoint) |
+| `--depth` | `1.33` | YOLOX backbone depth factor (1.33 for YOLOX-X) |
+| `--width` | `1.25` | YOLOX backbone width factor (1.25 for YOLOX-X) |
+
+#### GDRN
+
+```bash
+python tools/openvino/export_gdrn_openvino.py \
+    --ckpt output/gdrn/.../model_final_wo_optim.pth \
+    --output models/openvino/<gdrn_dir> \
+    --convert-mode pytorch-ov \
+    --verify
+```
+
+| Argument | Default | Description |
+|----------|---------|-------------|
+| `--ckpt` | (required) | Path to PyTorch checkpoint (.pth) |
+| `--output` | (required) | Output directory for IR files |
+| `--convert-mode` | `pytorch-ov` | Conversion path: `pytorch-onnx-ov` or `pytorch-ov` |
+| `--max-batch` | `8` | Upper bound for dynamic batch dimension |
+| `--fp16` | off | Compress weights to FP16 |
+| `--verify` | off | Verify OV output against PyTorch |
+
+The GDRN model is exported with 6 outputs: `pred_rot`, `pred_t`, `coor_x`, `coor_y`, `coor_z`, `vis_mask`.
+
+### Step 2: Run Inference
+
+#### Python API
+
+```python
+from gdrnpp_ov_pipeline import GDRNPPPipeline
+import cv2, numpy as np
+
+pipeline = GDRNPPPipeline(
+    yolox_model_path="models/openvino/<yolox_dir>/yolox.xml",
+    gdrn_model_path="models/openvino/<gdrn_dir>/gdrn.xml",
+    extents=extents,          # {cls_id: (3,) ndarray} object sizes in meters
+    cam_K=cam_K,              # (3,3) camera intrinsics
+    num_classes=8,
+    device="GPU",             # "CPU", "GPU", or "AUTO"
+    use_pnp=False,             # PnP RANSAC
+)
+
+image = cv2.imread("path/to/image.png")
+poses = pipeline(image)
+# poses: list of {"R": (3,3), "t": (3,), "score": float, "class_id": int}
+```
+With Pre-computed Detections (skip YOLOX)
+
+```python
+pipeline = GDRNPPPipeline(
+    yolox_model_path=None,    # no YOLOX needed
+    gdrn_model_path="models/openvino/<gdrn_dir>/gdrn.xml",
+    ...
+)
+
+bbox_list = [
+    {"bbox_est": [x1, y1, w, h], "obj_id": 1, "score": 0.95, "class_id": 0},
+    ...
+]
+poses = pipeline.run_from_bboxes(image, bbox_list)
+```
+
+
+| Parameter | Default | Description |
+|-----------|---------|-------------|
+| `device` | `"GPU"` | OpenVINO device: `"CPU"`, `"GPU"`, `"AUTO"` |
+| `use_pnp` | `False` | Use PnP RANSAC for pose from dense correspondences |
+| `mask_thr` | `0.5` | Visibility mask threshold for PnP point selection |
+| `conf_thr` | `0.01` | YOLOX detection confidence threshold |
+| `nms_thr` | `0.65` | YOLOX NMS IoU threshold |
+| `dzi_pad_scale` | `1.5` | ROI bounding box padding factor |
+| `depth_refine` | `False` | Enable depth-based translation refinement |
+| `refine_iter` | `2` | Depth refinement iterations |
+| `refine_thr` | `0.8` | Depth refinement confidence threshold |
+
+
+#### Performance Notes
+
+- **GDRN batch bucketing**: The pipeline uses fixed batch sizes (1, 4, 8) and pads inputs to the nearest bucket. This avoids GPU kernel recompilation on variable batch sizes.
+- **Warmup**: First inference per batch size triggers OpenCL kernel compilation. The pipeline runs warmup at init time.
+- **GPU model cache**: Set `CACHE_DIR` in OpenVINO Core properties to persist compiled kernels across runs (avoids slow first-start on GPU).
+
+#### Pose Output Format
+
+Each pose dict contains:
+
+```python
+{
+    "R": np.ndarray,      # (3, 3) rotation matrix
+    "t": np.ndarray,      # (3,) translation in meters
+    "score": float,       # detection confidence
+    "class_id": int,      # 0-indexed class (maps to LMO obj via LMO_OBJ_IDS)
+    "method": str,        # "pnp_ransac" or "direct"
+}
+```
+
+
+## LMO BOP Demo
+
+This demo runs GDRN on the BOP LM-O test split with the published detections. It
+is the shortest reproducible path because it skips YOLOX inference. Run every
+command from the repository root inside the `gdrnpp_dev` container.
+
+### Download the Pretrained Model and Detections
+
+The pretrained model is hosted in the
+[GDRNPP model repository](https://www.modelscope.cn/models/wangg12/GDRNPP). The
+[GDRNPP BOP22 test-bboxes dataset](https://www.modelscope.cn/datasets/wangg12/GDRNPP_bop22_test_bboxes)
+contains the published detections, not model weights. The commands below download
+only the two files needed by this demo instead of cloning the complete 73 GB
+model repository.
+
+```bash
+GDRN_DIR=output/gdrn/lmo_pbr/convnext_a6_AugCosyAAEGray_BG05_mlL1_DMask_amodalClipBox_classAware_lmo
+DET_DIR=datasets/BOP_DATASETS/lmo/test/test_bboxes
+
+mkdir -p "$GDRN_DIR" "$DET_DIR"
+
+curl -fL --retry 3 \
+    https://www.modelscope.cn/models/wangg12/GDRNPP/resolve/master/gdrn/lmo_pbr/convnext_a6_AugCosyAAEGray_BG05_mlL1_DMask_amodalClipBox_classAware_lmo/model_final_wo_optim.pth \
+    -o "$GDRN_DIR/model_final_wo_optim.pth"
+
+curl -fL --retry 3 \
+    https://www.modelscope.cn/datasets/wangg12/GDRNPP_bop22_test_bboxes/resolve/master/datasets/BOP_DATASETS/lmo/test/test_bboxes/yolox_x_640_lmo_pbr_lmo_bop_test.json \
+    -o "$DET_DIR/yolox_x_640_lmo_pbr_lmo_bop_test.json"
+```
+
+### Download the BOP LM-O Test Data
+
+Download the base metadata, object models, and BOP19 test subset from the
+[official BOP dataset repository](https://bop.felk.cvut.cz/datasets/):
+
+```bash
+REPO_ROOT=$PWD
+BOP_HUB=${BOP_HUB:-https://huggingface.co}
+mkdir -p /tmp/bop-lmo "$REPO_ROOT/datasets/BOP_DATASETS"
+
+curl -fL --retry 3 \
+    "$BOP_HUB/datasets/bop-benchmark/lmo/resolve/main/lmo_base.zip" \
+    -o /tmp/bop-lmo/lmo_base.zip
+curl -fL --retry 3 \
+    "$BOP_HUB/datasets/bop-benchmark/lmo/resolve/main/lmo_models.zip" \
+    -o /tmp/bop-lmo/lmo_models.zip
+curl -fL --retry 3 \
+    "$BOP_HUB/datasets/bop-benchmark/lmo/resolve/main/lmo_test_bop19.zip" \
+    -o /tmp/bop-lmo/lmo_test_bop19.zip
+
+python -m zipfile -e /tmp/bop-lmo/lmo_base.zip \
+    "$REPO_ROOT/datasets/BOP_DATASETS"
+python -m zipfile -e /tmp/bop-lmo/lmo_models.zip \
+    "$REPO_ROOT/datasets/BOP_DATASETS/lmo"
+python -m zipfile -e /tmp/bop-lmo/lmo_test_bop19.zip \
+    "$REPO_ROOT/datasets/BOP_DATASETS/lmo"
+```
+
+If `huggingface.co` is unavailable on your network, set a reachable Hugging Face
+mirror before running the block, for example
+`export BOP_HUB=https://hf-mirror.com`.
+
+The resulting data layout must include:
+
+```text
+datasets/BOP_DATASETS/lmo/
+├── models/models_info.json
+├── test/000002/rgb/
+├── test/000002/scene_camera.json
+├── test/test_bboxes/yolox_x_640_lmo_pbr_lmo_bop_test.json
+└── test_targets_bop19.json
+```
+
+### Export GDRN to OpenVINO IR
+
+```bash
+python tools/openvino/export_gdrn_openvino.py \
+    --ckpt output/gdrn/lmo_pbr/convnext_a6_AugCosyAAEGray_BG05_mlL1_DMask_amodalClipBox_classAware_lmo/model_final_wo_optim.pth \
+    --output models/openvino/gdrn_lmo \
+    --convert-mode pytorch-ov \
+    --fp16 \
+    --verify
+```
+
+This creates `models/openvino/gdrn_lmo/gdrn.xml` and `gdrn.bin`.
+
+### Optional: Export YOLOX to OpenVINO IR
+
+This step is not required when using the published detections from the previous
+section. Run it to execute the complete YOLOX detection and GDRN pose pipeline.
+
+```bash
+YOLOX_DIR=output/yolox/bop_pbr/yolox_x_640_augCozyAAEhsv_ranger_30_epochs_lmo_pbr_lmo_bop_test
+mkdir -p "$YOLOX_DIR"
+
+curl -fL --retry 3 \
+    https://www.modelscope.cn/models/wangg12/GDRNPP/resolve/master/yolox/bop_pbr/yolox_x_640_augCozyAAEhsv_ranger_30_epochs_lmo_pbr_lmo_bop_test/model_final.pth \
+    -o "$YOLOX_DIR/model_final.pth"
+
+python tools/openvino/export_yolox_openvino.py \
+    --ckpt "$YOLOX_DIR/model_final.pth" \
+    --output models/openvino/yolox_lmo \
+    --convert-mode pytorch-ov \
+    --fp16 \
+    --verify
+```
+
+This creates `models/openvino/yolox_lmo/yolox.xml` and `yolox.bin`.
+
+### Verify the OpenVINO GPU
+
+```bash
+python -c "from openvino import Core; print(Core().available_devices)"
+```
+
+The output must contain `GPU`. Use `--device CPU` in the next step if no Intel
+GPU is available.
+
+### Run the Demo
+
+```bash
+BOP_PATH=datasets/BOP_DATASETS \
+python tools/openvino/eval_bop_openvino.py \
+    --gdrn-model models/openvino/gdrn_lmo/gdrn.xml \
+    --det-file datasets/BOP_DATASETS/lmo/test/test_bboxes/yolox_x_640_lmo_pbr_lmo_bop_test.json \
+    --dataset-dir datasets/BOP_DATASETS/lmo \
+    --device GPU \
+    --output eval_output/lmo_openvino \
+    --profile \
+    --save-only
+```
+
+The demo writes the BOP-format predictions to
+`eval_output/lmo_openvino/gdrnpp-openvino-predet_lmo-test.csv` and per-image
+timings to `eval_output/lmo_openvino/timing_per_image.csv`. The arguments used
+for the run are saved to `eval_output/lmo_openvino/eval_args.json`. With
+`--profile`, the hierarchical stage summary is printed and also saved to
+`eval_output/lmo_openvino/profiling_report.txt`. Translation is converted from
+meters to millimeters automatically.
+
+After the prediction run succeeds, omit `--save-only` to invoke the bundled BOP
+scorer and calculate the default `ad,reteS,reS,teS` metrics:
+
+```bash
+BOP_PATH=datasets/BOP_DATASETS \
+python tools/openvino/eval_bop_openvino.py \
+    --gdrn-model models/openvino/gdrn_lmo/gdrn.xml \
+    --det-file datasets/BOP_DATASETS/lmo/test/test_bboxes/yolox_x_640_lmo_pbr_lmo_bop_test.json \
+    --dataset-dir datasets/BOP_DATASETS/lmo \
+    --device GPU \
+    --output eval_output/lmo_openvino
+```
+
+### Optional variants
+
+- Add `--use-pnp` to estimate poses from dense correspondences with PnP RANSAC.
+- Add `--depth-refine` to refine direct-regression translations with the LM-O
+  depth images and object models.
+- `--depth-refine` and `--use-pnp` are mutually exclusive.
+
+To run the complete detector-plus-pose pipeline after exporting YOLOX, replace
+`--det-file` with `--yolox-model`:
+
+```bash
+BOP_PATH=datasets/BOP_DATASETS \
+python tools/openvino/eval_bop_openvino.py \
+        --yolox-model models/openvino/yolox_lmo/yolox.xml \
+        --gdrn-model models/openvino/gdrn_lmo/gdrn.xml \
+        --dataset-dir datasets/BOP_DATASETS/lmo \
+        --device GPU \
+        --output eval_output/lmo_openvino_e2e \
+        --save-only
+```
+
+| Argument | Default | Description |
+|----------|---------|-------------|
+| `--gdrn-model` | (required) | Path to GDRN `.xml` |
+| `--yolox-model` | `None` | Path to YOLOX `.xml` (skip if `--det-file` is used) |
+| `--det-file` | `None` | Pre-computed detection JSON (skips YOLOX inference) |
+| `--det-score-thr` | `0.0` | Score threshold for pre-computed detections |
+| `--dataset-dir` | `datasets/BOP_DATASETS/lmo` | BOP dataset root |
+| `--output` | `eval_output/lmo_openvino` | Output directory for CSV and scores |
+| `--device` | `GPU` | OpenVINO device: `CPU`, `GPU`, `AUTO` |
+| `--use-pnp` | off | Toggle PnP RANSAC pose estimation |
+| `--mask-thr` | `0.5` | Visibility mask threshold for PnP |
+| `--depth-refine` | off | Enable depth-based translation refinement |
+| `--refine-iter` | `2` | Number of depth refinement iterations |
+| `--refine-thr` | `0.8` | Confidence threshold for depth refinement |
+| `--error-types` | `ad,reteS,reS,teS` | BOP error types to evaluate (comma-separated) |
+| `--save-only` | off | Only save predictions CSV, skip BOP evaluation |
+| `--profile` | off | Enable per-stage timing and save `profiling_report.txt` |
